<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Tovata Confederacy</h1><p class="st-meta">1867 CE – 1871 CE · capital Lomaloma</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A confederation of eastern Fiji built by the Tongan prince Enele Maʻafu, the main rival to Cakobau's power before Fiji was united.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enele-maafu">Enele Maʻafu</a>, a kinsman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-tupou-i">George Tupou I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-tonga">Kingdom of Tonga</a>, came to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fiji">Fiji</a> in 1847 to oversee the Tongans living there. Through warfare and alliances he became the dominant power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lau-islands">Lau Islands</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanua-levu">Vanua Levu</a>. In 1867 he and the chiefs of Lau, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cakaudrove-province">Cakaudrove</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bua-province">Bua</a> formed the Confederation of Lau, known as Tovata, with Lomaloma on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanua-balavu">Vanua Balavu</a> as its seat.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Tovata adopted a written constitution with a council of chiefs and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enele-maafu">Maʻafu</a> as its leading figure. It promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> of the Wesleyan kind, which Tongans had brought to eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fiji">Fiji</a>, and drew revenue from the trade in copra and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> with European planters and merchants. Its rivalry with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-bau">Kingdom of Bau</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seru-epenisa-cakobau">Cakobau</a> shaped Fijian politics.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1871 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enele-maafu">Maʻafu</a> agreed to join <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seru-epenisa-cakobau">Cakobau</a>'s new <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-fiji">Kingdom of Fiji</a> and became its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lau-islands">Lau</a>, ending Tovata. He signed the cession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fiji">Fiji</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> in 1874 and was recognised as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tui-lau">Tui Lau</a>, a title that survives.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tovata-confederacy.jpg" alt="Tovata Confederacy" width="320" height="186"><figcaption>Image: Jo5ta keresme · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tovata_flag.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1867 CE – 1871 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lomaloma</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Enele Maʻafu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Methodism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Fijian, Tongan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/fiji">Fiji</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Confederation of Lau, Tovata</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1869&amp;focus=tovata-confederacy" aria-label="Tovata Confederacy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="9540 2801 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tovata Confederacy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M9860 3057L9855 3090"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M9855 3090h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M9860 3057h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M9860 3057h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1869&amp;focus=tovata-confederacy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
